        "title": "feat(cron): declarative jobs with owner attribution and richer status",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nExtends canonical cron jobs with the capabilities #98727 built as a separate \"routines\" registry — as plain additive cron features, per the product decision that a routine is not a new concept. No new table, service, RPC namespace, or CLI noun.\n\n- **Declarative upsert**: `cron.add` gains optional `declarationKey`. Re-declaring the same key converges the existing job (schedule/payload/delivery/displayName, enablement only when explicitly set) in one store lock + write transaction — `{created:false, updated:true|false}` — preserving job id, run history, and current enablement. No staged-write state machines, no drift model: with one store there is nothing to drift from. Identity-adjacent fields (name, target, routing, owner) are deliberately outside convergence.\n- **Scope-local uniqueness + owner attribution**: declaration keys are unique within the caller's scope. Agent-scoped callers are bounded by gateway-owned `agentRuntimeIdentity` (structural, not marker-based) and get `owner` stamped automatically; operators may pass explicit owner. Owner is immutable attribution.\n- **Richer status on existing reads**: `declarationKey`, `displayName`, `owner`, `nextRunAtMs`, `lastRunAtMs/Status/Error`, last delivery and failure-notification outcomes — derived from existing job/run/delivery state only.\n- **Salvaged from #98727** (the parts that were always cron improvements): `cron-caller-scope.ts` and `cron-error-classification.ts` extractions (gateway `cron.ts` net −169), `delivery-channel-validation.ts` wired into add/converge (main-session jobs reject webhook delivery), update preconditions, and blank/duplicate-id validation.\n- Additive `cron_jobs` columns via the existing `ensureColumn` pattern; protocol schemas extended additively with regenerated JSON schema + Swift models (defaulted initializers keep source compat); `openclaw cron add` gains `--declaration-key` / `--display-name`; the cron agent tool extended in place.\n\n36 files, +1,784/−411 — replacing #98727's +6,539/−406 (51 files) for the same operator capability, minus the second concept.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `pnpm tsgo` clean (verified twice: implementation run + independent review run).\n- Vitest: 531 tests / 9 files green on the implementation run; independent re-run of the focused suites (declarative-jobs service, gateway cron validation, cron tool, cron CLI, server-cron-lazy) — 489/489.\n- `pnpm protocol:gen && protocol:gen:swift` — regeneration byte-identical post-commit.\n- oxfmt/oxlint clean on all changed files; autoreview clean, no actionable findings.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nTrigger-kind generalization (repository events, webhooks, channel-watch) is the intended follow-up on this same surface — a job's trigger becomes a kind, `schedule` being the first. No UI changes.\n\nSupersedes #98727.\n\n_Implemented by Codex (koffing-updated, high reasoning) from a frozen spec; reviewed and independently verified by Claude._\n",
